4520 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(-\\frac{\\ln x}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(-\\frac{\\ln x}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\ln x\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186674521 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\ln x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\ln x\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}