\\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{25}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186676540 :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 5 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{25(1-(\\frac{1}{5})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{\\frac{7}{4}}{\\sqrt{25 - 5 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{7}{20}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{7}{20}(\\sqrt{5})\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5}}{20}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{20}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5} \\right)}}{20}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 5 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{25\\left(1-\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)x^{2}\\right)}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{\\frac{7}{4}}{\\sqrt{25 - 5 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{7}{20}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5}\\right)^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{7}{20}(\\sqrt{5})\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5}}{20}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{20}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{7 \\sqrt{5} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} x}{5} \\right)}}{20}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186676553 :question/worked-solution "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 10 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{25(1-(\\frac{2}{5})x^{2})}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{10} x}{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{25 - 10 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{\\sqrt{10} x}{5})^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{5}(\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2})\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{10}}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{10} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{5}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{10} \\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{10} x}{5} \\right)}}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25 - 10 x^{2}}=\\sqrt{25\\left(1-\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)x^{2}\\right)}\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{\\sqrt{10} x}{5}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{5},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{25 - 10 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt